      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Glan</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Oesterreich kaernten-K.png|right|Klagenfurt in Carinthia]]
'''Klagenfurt''' ([[Slovenian language|Slovenian]] ''Celovec'') is the capital of the federal state of [[Carinthia (state)|Carinthia]] ([[German language|German]] ''Kärnten''),  in [[Austria]], on the [[Glan (Gurk)|Glan]] river. It is located at {{coor dm|46|37|N|14|19|E|}}. First settled in the [[12th century]], it currently has a population of approximately 90,000.

It is a popular vacation spot with mountains to both the south and north, numerous parks and a series of 23 castles on its outskirts. In summertime the city is home to the Altstadtzauber (The Magic of the Old City) festival, the [[Ironman]] Contest and the [[Ingeborg Bachmann Preis]], a prize for German literature.

The Old City with its central &quot;Alter Platz&quot; (Old Square) is also worth seeing. Notable landmarks include the [[Wörthersee]], the warmest European [[Alpine lake]], the [[Lindwurm Brunnen]] (a [[lindorm]] fountain), and nearby [[Hochosterwitz Castle]], an impressively fortified castle on a high hill that can only be reached by an ascending spiral path which is fortified with a series of gates.

Also located here are the [[University of Klagenfurt]] and [[Klagenfurt airport]]. Among other Austrian educational institutions, there is also the [[Slovenians|Slovenian]] non-classical [[Gymnasium (school)|Gymnasium]].

Famous residents include [[Joseph Stefan|Josef Stefan]], [[Robert Musil]]
and [[Ingeborg Bachmann]].
[[Image:Klagenfurt_Lend.jpg|thumb|right|View at the [[Lendkanal]] in the center of Klagenfurt]]
{{Carinthia}}

[[Category:Cities and towns in Austria]]

